The scalar constraints in the scalar sector give
\[
\delta\phi=nf(\delta\dot\vartheta-\dot\vartheta A),
\]
so the second ratio is one. The momentum constraint then gives
\[
A=\frac{\dot\vartheta\,\delta\vartheta}{2H},
\]
so the first ratio is one. Therefore the only nonzero prefactor surviving is
\[
\frac{1+3n^2f^2}{nf}.
\]
For \(n=0.5\) and \(f=1.7\),
\[
\frac{1+3n^2f^2}{nf}
=
\frac{1+3(0.5)^2(1.7)^2}{(0.5)(1.7)}
=\frac{1267}{340}
=3.726470588\ldots .
\]

\[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
&\frac{P_{\mathcal R}(1+3n^2f^2)}
{\left(\frac{H^2}{4\pi^2M_{\rm Pl}^2}\right)
 \left(\frac{H}{\dot\vartheta}\right)^2
 2^{2\nu-3}\left|
