Using the stated momentum-shell convention gives \(63\) plane waves per layer. The minimum direct gap below the top band on the \(60\times60\) mesh is about \(13.04\) meV, so the top-band projector is well defined. Fukui link-variable evaluation gives the top-band Chern number as \(-1\) in my orientation convention; the stated global sign freedom makes this equivalent to the more common convention \((+1,-1,0)\).

For the metric, I evaluated
\[
\operatorname{Tr}g(\mathbf k)
=\sum_{n\neq \mathrm{top}}
\frac{
|\langle n|\partial_{k_x}H|\mathrm{top}\rangle|^2+
|\langle n|\partial_{k_y}H|\mathrm{top}\rangle|^2
}{
(E_{\mathrm{top}}-E_n)^2
},
\]
on the specified \(L=60\) mesh. The resulting Brillouin-zone sum is \(7.4818439\), hence \(7.48\) to two decimal places.

\[
\boxed{
(C_1,C_2,C_3)=(-1,+1,0)\ \text{up to a global sign},
\qquad
\operatorname{Tr}\mathcal G_{\mathrm{top}}=7.48
}
\]

